@@ -3,4 +3,4 @@
     <link rel="alternate" hreflang="en" href="https://playpoint-sim.com/en/articles/google-play-points-use-coupons.html" />
     <link rel="alternate" hreflang="ko" href="https://playpoint-sim.com/ko/articles/google-play-points-use-coupons.html" />
     <link rel="alternate" hreflang="zh-TW" href="https://playpoint-sim.com/tw/articles/google-play-points-use-coupons.html" />
-    <link rel="alternate" hreflang="x-default" href="https://playpoint-sim.com/en/articles/google-play-points-use-coupons.html" /><link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/articles/article-shared.css?v=570302fe13"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/en/articles/intl-article.css?v=7e174d8811"><meta property="og:type" content="article"><meta property="og:site_name" content="Google Play Points Calculator"><meta property="og:title" content="How to use Google Play Points and coupons"><meta property="og:description" content="Redeem points without confusing coupons, Play credit, and cash."><meta property="og:url" content="https://playpoint-sim.com/en/articles/google-play-points-use-coupons.html"><meta property="og:image" content="https://playpoint-sim.com/ogp.png"><meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image"><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Article","headline":"How to use Google Play Points and coupons","description":"Learn how to redeem Google Play Points for coupons, Play credit, in-app items, and partner rewards, with expiration and refund checks.","url":"https://playpoint-sim.com/en/articles/google-play-points-use-coupons.html","inLanguage":"en","datePublished":"2026-07-25","dateModified":"2026-07-25","image":"https://playpoint-sim.com/ogp.png","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Katakata","url":"https://playpoint-sim.com/author/katakata.html"},"publisher":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Google Play Points Calculator","url":"https://playpoint-sim.com/","logo":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://playpoint-sim.com/favicon.svg"}}}</script><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Where is a coupon after I redeem it?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Google says it is saved under Notifications & offers in Saved offers. It should apply automatically to a qualifying in-app purchase."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do Play Points coupons expire?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Google says coupons exchanged with points expire after one year."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I undo an in-app item exchange?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Google says points used for in-app or in-game items generally cannot be refunded."}}]}</script></head><body><main class="main-card"><div class="hero"><span class="hero-badge">Using points</span><h1>How to use Google Play Points and coupons</h1><p class="hero-meta">Updated 2026-07-25 ・ Play Points guide</p></div><article class="content"><div class="intro">Google Play Points can be exchanged for several kinds of rewards, but they do not all work the same way. A coupon discounts a qualifying purchase, Play credit becomes a separate Google Play balance, and an in-app item is delivered inside a specific app or game. Check the target, minimum purchase, expiration, and refund rule before you spend points.</div><nav class="intl-article-toc" aria-label="Table of contents"><h2>Table of contents</h2><ol><li><a href="#section-1">Start from the Use tab</a></li><li><a href="#section-2">Coupons discount only qualifying purchases</a></li><li><a href="#section-3">Play credit is not the same as a coupon</a></li><li><a href="#section-4">In-app items and partner rewards have separate rules</a></li><li><a href="#section-5">Compare usefulness, not only the displayed value</a></li></ol></nav><section class="section"><h2 id="section-1">Start from the Use tab</h2><p>Open Google Play, choose the Google account that owns the points, open Play Points, and select Use. The rewards shown there are the options currently available to that account and country.</p><p>Do not rely on an old screenshot or another region's reward list. Availability and required points can change.</p></section><section class="section"><h2 id="section-2">Coupons discount only qualifying purchases</h2><p>A coupon applies automatically when an in-app or in-game purchase meets its conditions. Check the eligible app, minimum purchase amount, discount amount, and expiration before exchanging points.</p><p>Google says coupons exchanged with points expire after one year. A saved coupon can be found in Notifications &amp; offers under Saved offers, although menu wording may vary by app version.</p></section><section class="section"><h2 id="section-3">Play credit is not the same as a coupon</h2><p>Google Play credit can be used for eligible Google Play purchases, while an app-specific coupon is limited to the named app or game and its conditions.</p><p>Credit received by exchanging points expires after one year. It is not cash and cannot be withdrawn to a bank or external wallet.</p></section><section class="section"><h2 id="section-4">In-app items and partner rewards have separate rules</h2><p>An exchanged in-app or in-game item must be found inside the relevant app. Partner vouchers, when available, are usually stored in the Perks tab and may have their own redemption deadline.</p><p>Google says points used for in-app items or donations generally cannot be refunded, so confirm the destination before completing the exchange.</p></section><section class="section"><h2 id="section-5">Compare usefulness, not only the displayed value</h2><p>The best reward is the one you were already going to use. A large-looking coupon can be poor value if it requires an extra purchase or expires before you need it.</p><p>Keep point-earning cost and redemption value separate. The calculator estimates how much spending may earn points; it does not decide which reward is worth using.</p></section><div class="cta-box"><h3>Check how much spending may earn the points you need</h3><p>Estimate the earning side first, then choose a reward only when you know where it will be used.</p><a class="cta-btn" href="/en/">Open the calculator</a></div><aside class="official-source-note"><h2>Official sources</h2><p>Google's official help explains the Use tab, coupons, Play credit, in-app items, partner rewards, expiration, and refund limitations.</p><p><a href="https://support.google.com/googleplay/answer/9079840?hl=en" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Use points in the Google Play Store</a></p><p><a href="https://support.google.com/googleplay/answer/9077247?hl=en" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Play Points troubleshooting</a></p></aside><section class="section"><h2>FAQ</h2><h3>Where is a coupon after I redeem it?</h3><p>Google says it is saved under Notifications &amp; offers in Saved offers. It should apply automatically to a qualifying in-app purchase.</p><h3>Do Play Points coupons expire?</h3><p>Yes. Google says coupons exchanged with points expire after one year.</p><h3>Can I undo an in-app item exchange?</h3><p>Google says points used for in-app or in-game items generally cannot be refunded.</p></section><section class="section related-links-section"><h2>Next step</h2><ul><li><a href="/en/articles/google-play-points-join-eligibility.html">Join requirements and missing Join button</a></li><li><a href="/en/articles/google-play-points-cash-conversion.html">Why Play credit is not cash</a></li><li><a href="/en/articles/google-play-points-expiration.html">Point and reward expiration</a></li><li><a href="/en/points-cost/">Points-to-cost calculator</a></li><li><a href="/author/katakata.html">Katakata</a></li></ul></section></article><aside class="author-box" aria-label="Article author"><p class="author-box-label">Article author</p><p class="author-box-name"><a href="/author/katakata.html" rel="author">Katakata</a> - Google Play Points Calculator</p><p>This guide separates official rules from practical planning. Confirm the current options and eligibility in the Google Play app before acting.</p></aside><footer class="article-footer"><p><a href="/en/articles/">Back to guides</a> | <a href="/en/">Calculator top</a></p></footer></main><script src="/js/intent-tracking.js?v=5cdd51c178"></script><script src="/js/third-party.js?v=30f1e46c0b"></script></body></html>
